INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Mandiant, Zero-Day Vulnerability in MOVEit Transfer Exploited for Data Theft", "source_url": "https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-158a", "text": "SRC-001 raw text reports: Progress announced the MOVEit Transfer vulnerability on May 31, 2023 and it was assigned CVE-2023-34362. Earliest observed exploitation was May 27, 2023, involving web-shell deployment and data theft; some theft occurred within minutes. Actors deployed the newly discovered C# LEMURLOOT web shell, often named human.aspx/human2.aspx/_human2.aspx to masquerade as legitimate software. LEMURLOOT could enumerate files/folders, retrieve configuration and database/file information, retrieve files, access Azure Blob settings including credentials, and create/delete a Health Check Service user. Mandiant observed SQL-injection POST requests to guestaccess.aspx, scanning/exploitation from 5.252.188.0/22, and second-stage systems with RDP services and certificates generated May 19-22. The campaign affected organizations in Canada, India, and the U.S.; public repositories suggested Italy, Pakistan, and Germany, while overall impact was likely broader. Mandiant initially attributed activity to UNC4857, then on June 6 merged UNC4857 into FIN11 based on targeting, infrastructure, certificate, and data-leak-site overlaps. Mandiant assessed activity as consistent with extortion actors; victims initially received no ransom demands. On June 5 Bleeping Computer reported an alleged CLOP-affiliated statement; on June 6 the CL0P^_-LEAKS data leak site claimed responsibility and threatened publication unless an extortion fee was paid. Mandiant said it had not directly observed extortion emails to confirmed victims. It assessed the activity as reminiscent of prior FIN11-attributed data-theft/extortion campaigns involving Accellion FTA/DEWMODE and GoAnywhere MFT CVE-2023-0669, and noted an exploitation IP had been used by FIN11 in January 2023 and retained the same RDP certificate. SRC-002 NVD describes CVE-2023-34362 as an unauthenticated SQL injection in MOVEit Transfer allowing database access and potentially SQL statements that alter/delete database elements; it was exploited in the wild in May and June 2023 via HTTP/HTTPS. NVD lists CVSS 3.1 9.8 Critical, CWE-89, affected pre-patch versions, NVD published date 2023-06-02, CISA KEV addition 2023-06-02 with due date 2023-06-23, and required action to apply vendor updates."}
